{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"fdb20c835c9a0b9f323da0e0","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260805231041.3791771-1-matthew.brost%40intel.com/","channels":["lkml"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260805231041.3791771-1-matthew.brost@intel.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260805231041.3791771-1-matthew.brost%40intel.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260805231041.3791771-1-matthew.brost@intel.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v3 4/6] drm/pagemap: dma-unmap pages before handling migration errors","messages":{"9e986d7c-d561-4a63-8b14-6380ac289db5@intel.com":{"id":"9e986d7c-d561-4a63-8b14-6380ac289db5@intel.com","messageId":"9e986d7c-d561-4a63-8b14-6380ac289db5@intel.com","references":["20260805231041.3791771-1-matthew.brost@intel.com","20260805231041.3791771-5-matthew.brost@intel.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260805231041.3791771-5-matthew.brost@intel.com","20260805231041.3791771-1-matthew.brost@intel.com"],"author":{"name":"Ghimiray, Himal Prasad","address":"himal.prasad.ghimiray@intel.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Matthew Brost","address":"matthew.brost@intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"intel-xe@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"name":"","address":"dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-mm@kvack.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Sashiko","address":"sashiko-bot@kernel.org"},{"name":"Andrew Morton","address":"akpm@linux-foundation.org"},{"name":"David Hildenbrand","address":"david@kernel.org"},{"name":"Lorenzo Stoakes","address":"ljs@kernel.org"},{"name":"Zi Yan","address":"ziy@nvidia.com"},{"name":"Baolin Wang","address":"baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com"},{"name":"Liam R . Howlett","address":"liam@infradead.org"},{"name":"Nico Pache","address":"nico.pache@linux.dev"},{"name":"Ryan Roberts","address":"ryan.roberts@arm.com"},{"name":"Dev Jain","address":"dev.jain@arm.com"},{"name":"Barry Song","address":"baohua@kernel.org"},{"name":"Lance Yang","address":"lance.yang@linux.dev"},{"name":"Usama Arif","address":"usama.arif@linux.dev"},{"name":"Joshua Hahn","address":"joshua.hahnjy@gmail.com"},{"name":"Rakie Kim","address":"rakie.kim@sk.com"},{"name":"Byungchul Park","address":"byungchul@sk.com"},{"name":"Gregory Price","address":"gourry@gourry.net"},{"name":"Ying Huang","address":"ying.huang@linux.alibaba.com"},{"name":"Alistair Popple","address":"apopple@nvidia.com"},{"name":"Balbir Singh","address":"balbirs@nvidia.com"},{"name":"Maarten Lankhorst","address":"maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com"},{"name":"Maxime Ripard","address":"mripard@kernel.org"},{"name":"Thomas Zimmermann","address":"tzimmermann@suse.de"},{"name":"David Airlie","address":"airlied@gmail.com"},{"name":"Simona Vetter","address":"simona@ffwll.ch"},{"name":"Thomas Hellström","address":"thomas.hellstrom@linux.intel.com"},{"name":"Francois Dugast","address":"francois.dugast@intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T15:04:06.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T15:04:06.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v3 4/6] drm/pagemap: dma-unmap pages before handling migration errors","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 06-08-2026 04:40, Matthew Brost wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"drm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages() relies on the pages array to determine"},{"depth":1,"text":"which pages require DMA unmapping. However,"},{"depth":1,"text":"drm_pagemap_migration_unlock_put_pages() clears the array as part of its"},{"depth":1,"text":"cleanup, leaving drm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages() with no valid page"},{"depth":1,"text":"information if it is called afterward."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Call drm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages() before"},{"depth":1,"text":"drm_pagemap_migration_unlock_put_pages() so the pages array remains"},{"depth":1,"text":"valid during DMA unmapping."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Fixes: f86ad0ed620c (\"drm/gpusvm, drm/pagemap: Move migration functionality to drm_pagemap\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Baolin Wang <baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Liam R. Howlett <liam@infradead.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Nico Pache <nico.pache@linux.dev>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Ryan Roberts <ryan.roberts@arm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Dev Jain <dev.jain@arm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Barry Song <baohua@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Lance Yang <lance.yang@linux.dev>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Usama Arif <usama.arif@linux.dev>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Joshua Hahn <joshua.hahnjy@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Rakie Kim <rakie.kim@sk.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Byungchul Park <byungchul@sk.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Ying Huang <ying.huang@linux.alibaba.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Alistair Popple <apopple@nvidia.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Balbir Singh <balbirs@nvidia.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Maarten Lankhorst <maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Maxime Ripard <mripard@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Thomas Zimmermann <tzimmermann@suse.de>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: David Airlie <airlied@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Simona Vetter <simona@ffwll.ch>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Thomas Hellström <thomas.hellstrom@linux.intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Francois Dugast <francois.dugast@intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: linux-mm@kvack.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Matthew Brost <matthew.brost@intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":"  drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c | 12 ++++++------"},{"depth":1,"text":"  1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 892b325fa99b..aef1fcea663d 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1175,12 +1175,12 @@ int drm_pagemap_evict_to_ram(struct drm_pagemap_devmem *devmem_allocation)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tgoto err_finalize;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   err_finalize:"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tdrm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages(devmem_allocation->dev, pagemap_addr, dst, npages,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\tDMA_FROM_DEVICE, &state);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tif (err)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tdrm_pagemap_migration_unlock_put_pages(npages, dst);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tmigrate_device_pages(src, dst, npages);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tmigrate_device_finalize(src, dst, npages);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tdrm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages(devmem_allocation->dev, pagemap_addr, dst, npages,"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t\t\t\tDMA_FROM_DEVICE, &state);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   err_free:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tkvfree(buf);"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1305,14 +1305,14 @@ static int __drm_pagemap_migrate_to_ram(struct vm_area_struct *vas,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tgoto err_finalize;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   err_finalize:"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tif (err)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tdrm_pagemap_migration_unlock_put_pages(npages, migrate.dst);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tmigrate_vma_pages(&migrate);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tmigrate_vma_finalize(&migrate);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tif (dev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tdrm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages(dev, pagemap_addr, migrate.dst,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\t\t\t\t\tnpages, DMA_FROM_DEVICE,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\t\t\t\t\t&state);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tif (err)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tdrm_pagemap_migration_unlock_put_pages(npages, migrate.dst);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tmigrate_vma_pages(&migrate);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tmigrate_vma_finalize(&migrate);"}],"lineCount":76,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"LGTM\nReviewed-by: Himal Prasad Ghimiray <himal.prasad.ghimiray@intel.com>"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"  err_free:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tkvfree(buf);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  err_out:"}],"lineCount":3,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260805231041.3791771-5-matthew.brost@intel.com"},"0e197017-7054-468a-b641-1b5a00d77db2@intel.com":{"id":"0e197017-7054-468a-b641-1b5a00d77db2@intel.com","messageId":"0e197017-7054-468a-b641-1b5a00d77db2@intel.com","references":["20260805231041.3791771-1-matthew.brost@intel.com","20260805231041.3791771-6-matthew.brost@intel.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260805231041.3791771-6-matthew.brost@intel.com","20260805231041.3791771-1-matthew.brost@intel.com"],"author":{"name":"Ghimiray, Himal Prasad","address":"himal.prasad.ghimiray@intel.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Matthew Brost","address":"matthew.brost@intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"intel-xe@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"name":"","address":"dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-mm@kvack.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"Andrew Morton","address":"akpm@linux-foundation.org"},{"name":"David Hildenbrand","address":"david@kernel.org"},{"name":"Lorenzo Stoakes","address":"ljs@kernel.org"},{"name":"Zi Yan","address":"ziy@nvidia.com"},{"name":"Baolin Wang","address":"baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com"},{"name":"Liam R . Howlett","address":"liam@infradead.org"},{"name":"Nico Pache","address":"nico.pache@linux.dev"},{"name":"Ryan Roberts","address":"ryan.roberts@arm.com"},{"name":"Dev Jain","address":"dev.jain@arm.com"},{"name":"Barry Song","address":"baohua@kernel.org"},{"name":"Lance Yang","address":"lance.yang@linux.dev"},{"name":"Usama Arif","address":"usama.arif@linux.dev"},{"name":"Joshua Hahn","address":"joshua.hahnjy@gmail.com"},{"name":"Rakie Kim","address":"rakie.kim@sk.com"},{"name":"Byungchul Park","address":"byungchul@sk.com"},{"name":"Gregory Price","address":"gourry@gourry.net"},{"name":"Ying Huang","address":"ying.huang@linux.alibaba.com"},{"name":"Alistair Popple","address":"apopple@nvidia.com"},{"name":"Balbir Singh","address":"balbirs@nvidia.com"},{"name":"Maarten Lankhorst","address":"maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com"},{"name":"Maxime Ripard","address":"mripard@kernel.org"},{"name":"Thomas Zimmermann","address":"tzimmermann@suse.de"},{"name":"David Airlie","address":"airlied@gmail.com"},{"name":"Simona Vetter","address":"simona@ffwll.ch"},{"name":"Thomas Hellström","address":"thomas.hellstrom@linux.intel.com"},{"name":"Francois Dugast","address":"francois.dugast@intel.com"},{"name":"","address":"stable@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T15:36:44.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T15:36:44.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v3 5/6] drm/pagemap: Fix folio allocation fallback and use-after-put","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On 06-08-2026 04:40, Matthew Brost wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_ram_pfn() had two issues when populating"},{"depth":1,"text":"RAM PFNs with higher-order folios:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> 1. The higher-order vma_alloc_folio()/folio_alloc() calls did not pass"},{"depth":1,"text":"    __GFP_NOWARN, so a THP allocation failure under memory pressure"},{"depth":1,"text":"    would spam the kernel log, and there was no fallback path despite a"},{"depth":1,"text":"    TODO comment stating one was needed. Add __GFP_NOWARN to the"},{"depth":1,"text":"    higher-order allocation and, on failure, fall back to order-0"},{"depth":1,"text":"    allocations for the entire range originally covered by the failed"},{"depth":1,"text":"    higher-order allocation, leaving MIGRATE_PFN_COMPOUND unset for"},{"depth":1,"text":"    those PFNs."},{"depth":1,"text":"> 2. In the free_pages error path, order was computed via"},{"depth":1,"text":"    folio_order(page_folio(page)) *after* put_page(page) had already"},{"depth":1,"text":"    dropped the reference, resulting in a use-after-free/put when that"},{"depth":1,"text":"    was the last reference on the page. Compute order before releasing"},{"depth":1,"text":"    the page."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Introducing the fallback in 1. also requires the source page array"},{"depth":1,"text":"handed to ->copy_to_ram() to be built differently. Both callers only"},{"depth":1,"text":"populated the entry at the head of each source folio, relying on the"},{"depth":1,"text":"copy callback to derive the rest of the folio from the order recorded"},{"depth":1,"text":"in the matching drm_pagemap_addr. Once the destination has been demoted"},{"depth":1,"text":"to order-0 folios the drm_pagemap_addr entries are per-page, so a source"},{"depth":1,"text":"page is needed for every one of them; leaving them NULL makes the copy"},{"depth":1,"text":"callback stop after the first page and the remainder of the range is"},{"depth":1,"text":"never copied."},{"depth":1,"text":"> The source folio is only split later, by migrate_vma_pages() /"},{"depth":1,"text":"migrate_device_pages(), so its order cannot be used to detect the"},{"depth":1,"text":"demotion - test the destination for MIGRATE_PFN_COMPOUND instead. Factor"},{"depth":1,"text":"the array population out into drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_src_pages()"},{"depth":1,"text":"and use it from both drm_pagemap_evict_to_ram() and"},{"depth":1,"text":"__drm_pagemap_migrate_to_ram()."},{"depth":1,"text":"> Fixes: ddeda6136038 (\"drm/pagemap: Allocate folios when possible\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: David Hildenbrand <david@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Lorenzo Stoakes <ljs@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Zi Yan <ziy@nvidia.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Baolin Wang <baolin.wang@linux.alibaba.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Liam R. Howlett <liam@infradead.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Nico Pache <nico.pache@linux.dev>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Ryan Roberts <ryan.roberts@arm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Dev Jain <dev.jain@arm.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Barry Song <baohua@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Lance Yang <lance.yang@linux.dev>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Usama Arif <usama.arif@linux.dev>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Joshua Hahn <joshua.hahnjy@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Rakie Kim <rakie.kim@sk.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Byungchul Park <byungchul@sk.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Gregory Price <gourry@gourry.net>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Ying Huang <ying.huang@linux.alibaba.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Alistair Popple <apopple@nvidia.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Balbir Singh <balbirs@nvidia.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Maarten Lankhorst <maarten.lankhorst@linux.intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Maxime Ripard <mripard@kernel.org>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Thomas Zimmermann <tzimmermann@suse.de>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: David Airlie <airlied@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Simona Vetter <simona@ffwll.ch>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Thomas Hellström <thomas.hellstrom@linux.intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: Francois Dugast <francois.dugast@intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: dri-devel@lists.freedesktop.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: linux-mm@kvack.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org"},{"depth":1,"text":"Assisted-by: GitHub_Copilot:claude-opus-5"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Matthew Brost <matthew.brost@intel.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"> ---"},{"depth":1,"text":"  v2: Add THP-mid-PMD invariant (Sashiko)"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":"  drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c | 128 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------"},{"depth":1,"text":"  1 file changed, 103 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index aef1fcea663d..51c6f12e4256 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_pagemap.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -383,6 +383,58 @@ drm_pagemap_migrate_map_system_pages(struct device *dev,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  }"},{"depth":1,"text":"  > +/**"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_src_pages() - Populate the source page array"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * @pages: Array of source pages to populate"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * @src_mpfn: Source array of migrate PFNs"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * @dst_mpfn: Destination array of migrate PFNs"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * @npages: Number of pages in the arrays"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ *"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * Populate @pages with the device pages the copy callback is to read from."},{"depth":1,"text":"+ *"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * Entries are normally only populated at the head of each source folio, with"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * the copy callback deriving the rest of the folio from the order recorded in"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * the corresponding drm_pagemap_addr. That does not work where"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_ram_pfn() had to demote a higher-order source"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * folio to order-0 destination folios: the drm_pagemap_addr entries are then"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * per-page, and the copy callback needs a source page for each of them."},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * Populate every entry for those ranges."},{"depth":1,"text":"+ *"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * Note that the source folio itself is only split later, by"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * migrate_vma_pages() / migrate_device_pages(), so its order cannot be used to"},{"depth":1,"text":"+ * detect the demotion - the destination has to be inspected instead."},{"depth":1,"text":"+ */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+static void drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_src_pages(struct page **pages,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\t\t   unsigned long *src_mpfn,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\t\t   unsigned long *dst_mpfn,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\t\t   unsigned long npages)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tunsigned long i;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tfor (i = 0; i < npages;) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tstruct page *page = migrate_pfn_to_page(src_mpfn[i]);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tunsigned int order = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tunsigned long j, nr;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tif (!page) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\ti++;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tcontinue;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\torder = folio_order(page_folio(page));"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tnr = NR_PAGES(order);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tif (order && !(dst_mpfn[i] & MIGRATE_PFN_COMPOUND)) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tfor (j = 0; j < nr && i + j < npages; j++)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\tpages[i + j] = folio_page(page_folio(page), j);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t} else {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tpages[i] = page;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\ti += nr;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"  /**"},{"depth":1,"text":"   * drm_pagemap_migrate_unmap_pages() - Unmap pages previously mapped for GPU SVM migration"},{"depth":1,"text":"   * @dev: The device for which the pages were mapped"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -875,6 +927,7 @@ static int drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_ram_pfn(struct vm_area_struct *vas,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tstruct page *page = NULL, *src_page;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tstruct folio *folio;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tunsigned int order = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tgfp_t gfp = GFP_HIGHUSER;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \t\tif (!(src_mpfn[i] & MIGRATE_PFN_MIGRATE))"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\t\tgoto next;"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -891,11 +944,51 @@ static int drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_ram_pfn(struct vm_area_struct *vas,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \t\torder = folio_order(page_folio(src_page));"},{"depth":1,"text":"  > -\t\t/* TODO: Support fallback to single pages if THP allocation fails */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * A large source folio is always collected whole, at its head"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * page, PMD aligned and flagged MIGRATE_PFN_COMPOUND: anything"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * else is split before it reaches us, either by"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * migrate_vma_collect_pmd() or, for the eviction path, by"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * migrate_device_pfns(). Both the order-0 fallback below and"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_src_pages() rely on that, as"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t * they index the folio from @i."},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tWARN_ON_ONCE(order &&"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t     (src_page != folio_page(page_folio(src_page), 0) ||"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t      !(src_mpfn[i] & MIGRATE_PFN_COMPOUND)));"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tif (order)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tgfp |= __GFP_NOWARN;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tif (vas)"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t\tfolio = vma_alloc_folio(GFP_HIGHUSER, order, vas, addr);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tfolio = vma_alloc_folio(gfp, order, vas, addr);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\telse"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t\tfolio = folio_alloc(GFP_HIGHUSER, order);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tfolio = folio_alloc(gfp, order);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tif (!folio && order) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t/*"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * Higher-order allocation failed, fall back to"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * order-0 allocations for the entire range covered"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * by the original higher-order allocation, without"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * setting MIGRATE_PFN_COMPOUND, until we move past"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t * that range."},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tunsigned long nr = NR_PAGES(order);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tunsigned long j;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tgfp &= ~__GFP_NOWARN;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tfor (j = 0; j < nr && i < npages; j++, i++, addr += PAGE_SIZE) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\tfolio = vas ?"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\tvma_alloc_folio(gfp, 0, vas, addr) :"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\tfolio_alloc(gfp, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\tif (!folio)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\t\tgoto free_pages;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\tpage = folio_page(folio, 0);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t\tmpfn[i] = migrate_pfn(page_to_pfn(page));"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t\tcontinue;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \t\tif (!folio)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\t\tgoto free_pages;"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -940,11 +1033,11 @@ static int drm_pagemap_migrate_populate_ram_pfn(struct vm_area_struct *vas,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tif (!page)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\t\tgoto next_put;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  > +\t\torder = folio_order(page_folio(page));"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tput_page(page);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tmpfn[i] = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  > -\t\torder = folio_order(page_folio(page));"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"  next_put:"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\ti += NR_PAGES(order);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1120,7 +1213,7 @@ int drm_pagemap_evict_to_ram(struct drm_pagemap_devmem *devmem_allocation)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tunsigned long *src, *dst;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tstruct drm_pagemap_addr *pagemap_addr;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tvoid *buf;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tint i, err = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tint err = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tunsigned int retry_count = 2;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \tnpages = devmem_allocation->size >> PAGE_SHIFT;"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1160,15 +1253,7 @@ int drm_pagemap_evict_to_ram(struct drm_pagemap_devmem *devmem_allocation)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tif (err)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tgoto err_finalize;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  > -\tfor (i = 0; i < npages;) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tunsigned int order = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tpages[i] = migrate_pfn_to_page(src[i]);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tif (pages[i])"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t\torder = folio_order(page_folio(pages[i]));"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\ti += NR_PAGES(order);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tdrm_pagemap_migrate_populate_src_pages(pages, src, dst, npages);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \terr = ops->copy_to_ram(pages, pagemap_addr, npages, NULL);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tif (err)"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1235,7 +1320,7 @@ static int __drm_pagemap_migrate_to_ram(struct vm_area_struct *vas,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tstruct drm_pagemap_addr *pagemap_addr;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tunsigned long start, end;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tvoid *buf;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tint i, err = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tint err = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \tzdd = drm_pagemap_page_zone_device_data(page);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tif (time_before64(get_jiffies_64(), zdd->devmem_allocation->timeslice_expiration))"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1290,15 +1375,8 @@ static int __drm_pagemap_migrate_to_ram(struct vm_area_struct *vas,"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tif (err)"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \t\tgoto err_finalize;"},{"depth":1,"text":"  > -\tfor (i = 0; i < npages;) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tunsigned int order = 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tpages[i] = migrate_pfn_to_page(migrate.src[i]);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\tif (pages[i])"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\t\torder = folio_order(page_folio(pages[i]));"},{"depth":1,"text":"-"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t\ti += NR_PAGES(order);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tdrm_pagemap_migrate_populate_src_pages(pages, migrate.src, migrate.dst,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t"}],"lineCount":246,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"LGTM\nReviewed-by: Himal Prasad Ghimiray <himal.prasad.ghimiray@intel.com>"},{"kind":"code","text":"\t\t\t\t       npages);"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"  >   \terr = ops->copy_to_ram(pages, pagemap_addr, npages, NULL);"},{"depth":1,"text":"  \tif (err)"}],"lineCount":2,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260805231041.3791771-6-matthew.brost@intel.com"}},"rootIds":["9e986d7c-d561-4a63-8b14-6380ac289db5@intel.com","0e197017-7054-468a-b641-1b5a00d77db2@intel.com"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["9e986d7c-d561-4a63-8b14-6380ac289db5@intel.com","0e197017-7054-468a-b641-1b5a00d77db2@intel.com"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}